// ─── 7. GO-LIVE RUNBOOK (shadow → live) — one switch, pre-audited pre-flip ───
// Runbook deliverable only. EXECUTION requires explicit rmw3 (S5) approval (D-GOLIVE-ANTICIPATION-01
// decision ID). NOT for
  autonomous use by DS or Claude.
// debt(S4-GOLIVE-UNSIGNED, class=human, owner=rmw3, gate=D-GOLIVE-ANTICIPATION-01)
// The whole anticipatory arc is BUILT, tested and DISCONNECTED. The flip is
// one env line; what is missing is the S5 signature, ¬the engineering.
// Explicitly ¬for autonomous use by DS or by me — the runbook says so and
// this marker makes it queryable.
// Behind it sits PHI-UP-PIPELINE: until the kernel reads the projection,
// flipping the switch would put a production flag on a loop with ∄ input.
go_live: {
  the_flip: "ONE line in @nucleus_wrapper on
                    LXC101: +export
             S3_ANTICIPATION_MODE=production (the binary defaults to SYNTHETIC when unset; env read
             at startup in start_directive_subscriber() → state.set_production() → self.synthetic=false).
             Deploy: `pct exec 101 --
               bash -c 'printf "export S3_ANTICIPATION_MODE=production\n"
               >>
             @nucleus_wrapper'` then restart vsf-nucleus-operational.",
  consequences: [
    "select_donor enforces stasis_cos ≥ 0.875 (BASIN_FLOOR) instead of the 50 weight proxy",
    "the ViabilityTracker monitors post-grant zone health ≥ 0.875 on donor and target (gap_2)",
    "weight changes logged REAL (not SYNTHETIC)",
    "Component B (vsf-cgroup-reallocate, host) reads the order files this binary writes and values
     serializes REAL cgroup weight changes
       — the flip now produces
       real writes, the single switch
     remains the kernel's emission; B
       is the actuator that consumes
       it.",
  ],
  preflight_2x: [
    "2.1 hardening-gate tests pass on HEAD (cargo test, 18)",
    "2.2 vsf-s3-star tests pass (50)",
    "2.3 PHI-UP-PIPELINE flowing: CAT stale-check on the L2 projection FILE ts — <70min (the L2
         aggregated file, NOT the raw L3-keyed — source updates hourly, so it is fresh)",
    "2.4 no 'pending_human' anticipation rows in the algedonic ledger",
    "2.5 current binary on 101 == the HEAD being deployed (sha check)",
    "2.6 cgroup v2 reachability: ls /sys/fs/cgroup/lxc/112 + service tree (grep the cgroup path, NOT
         the old v1 path)",
  ],
  rollback: "remove the env line (sed
                    -i '/export S3_ANTICIPATION_MODE=production/d' wrapper) +
             restart → binary falls back
               to SYNTHETIC. Verify: journal shows 'SYNTHETIC mode' +
             systemctl is-active. If rollback itself
               fails: rewrite to synthetic + restart; worst
             case redeploy the previous binary
               from 108.",
  monitoring_window_first_30min: [
    "4.1 kernel log: REAL mode line",
    "4.2 first directive handled GRANT ends 'REAL'",
    "4.3 no new anticipation pending_human in the ledger (escalations inspected)",
    "4.4 S3-star anticipation probe — no findings in the first cycle (else kernel self-check and
         S3* disagree — instantaneous investigation)",
    "4.5 Component B data is being applied: systemctl is-active vsf-cgroup-reallocate.timer + units'
         CPUWeight readback agrees with the
           order/delta",
    "4.6 per-zone current_sc from the L2 file ≥ baseline visual check — drops below 0.875 during
         the current stress window are
           EXPECTED stress, the floor was
           deliberately NOT recalibrated
         against the worst case (use the history logger for a post-storm recalibration instead)",
    "4.7 no panics/fatals + service stays active the whole time",
  ],
  sign_off: "Approver: rmw3 (S5, human). Decision-ID: D-GOLIVE-ANTICIPATION-01. Preflight passes:
           []; Post-flip passes: []; Rollback tested: []. Absent approval → the runbook remains
           documentation only.",
}

// ─── 8. THE FORECASTERS — the S1 weather-projection live-state fix (2026-07-03) ───
forecaster: {
  problem: "s4_markov_projection.json returned current_bin=+1, current_sc=NaN for
                    ALL zones — there
         was NO internal forecast, so
           DS had to fall back
           to external weather APIs.",
  diagnosis_live: "training OK (markov_T exists /var/lib/vsf-clima/markov/*.json) · bridge OK
         (s4-mailbridge relays faithfully, relay=NaN) → ROOT: markov_project.py reads CURRENT
         stasis_cos from /var/lib/vsf-clima/blob state/ root {zone}.json, which was EMPTY
         (only oni_current.json) — climate_kernel not writing the snapshot ⟹ current_sc=NaN.",
  correction: "the live current_sc ALREADY EXISTS
                    — OUR OWN kernels compute it
         (kernel_r32.py::stasis_cos(vec, omega, month); l2_zone.py aggregates the L3 φ↑). The
         forecast uses OUR OWN viability
           signal, flowing NOW through the
           climate φ-source blend.
         External ERA5 is only for the historical calibration (done); retract the external-API path.",
  what_it_forecasts: "the Markov projection forecasts the
                    VIABILITY REGIME trajectory (P of a zone
         drifting toward its Ω boundary within n steps) over 5 bins — NOT weather. A
         meteorological forecast is a DIFFERENT question (external API is the right tool for THAT;
         not redundant).",
  fix_wiring: "refactor markov_project.py to IMPORT the domain-agnostic core
         (@forecaster_py — train() + project() + sc_to_bin) and feed
         project() the CURRENT per-zone stasis_cos from the live φ↑ (L3 station NATS or the
         s4_clima_bundle events) — not state/ snapshots, not external API. ZoneStateCache seeds
         from /var/log/vsf-clima/{zone}.theta_up.jsonl on start (tail / cold-start), then live
         NATS keeps it current; fallback
           NaN after 24h stale.",
  acceptance: "≥ 10/12 zones show current_bin
                    ∈ {1..5} (not −1) and
                    a finite current_sc; at least
         one multi-step projection produces a
           non-degenerate distribution. VERIFIED 2026-07-03:
         12/12 zones, sc ∈ [−0.4997, 0.7933], non-degenerate T^n, P(exc_7d) ∈ [69.52%, 90.42%],
         multi_zone_alert=True — the wiring RESOLVED,
           but the calibration is still
           wrong below.",
  calibration_finding__ALTA: "the T matrix is so
                    skewed to low bins that
                    P(exc,7d)=0.759 for EVERY
         current state (degenerate). ALSO bins mis-scaled: a normal JULY day reads stasis_cos≈0.80
         = bin 2 (excursion!) — the dist=|x−μ|/half_range formula normalizes by range, not σ:
         normal weather is treated as
           excursion. PLUS the stationary pi
           was saved empty (train-format bug).
         // debt(FORECASTER-RECALIBRATE, class=experiment, owner=DS, gate=PHI-UP-PIPELINE)
         // TWO defects, not one: dist=|x−μ|/half_range normalizes by RANGE, not σ,
         // so a normal day is classified as an excursion; and the stationary
         // π was saved EMPTY (train-format bug). Per-zone σ-normalization is
         // a HARD gate — an anticipation that fires on normal weather is
         // worse than none, because it trains the operator to ignore it.
         ⟹ wiring alone is NOT enough: task FORECASTER-RECALIBRATE (per-zone
         σ-normalization so a typical day lands bin 4-5, 30mm day lands bin 1, T^n discriminates)
         is a HARD gate before
           this forecast is trusted.",
  honesty_guardrails: [
    "it forecasts a Viability-REGIME, not the weather",
    "the forecast is as good as the live feed + the 30-yr prior — say so",
    "meteorological answering stays with the external weather API — not redundant, not silent",
  ],
}

// ─── 9. THE COGNITIVE / CRAG LAYER — retrieval-augmented S4 functions (r-1) ───
// s4_intelligence.md defines 5 functions
  (EP/AC/SD/SA/EV) + the CRAG store;
  its Ax: the LLM is
// routed by function, and
  the algedonic channel is DETERMINISTIC
  (D6 ▪ R10).
crag: {
  axiom: "an LLM never sits inside
                    a latency- or safety-critical signal
                    path. The algedonic channel
         (S1→S5) uses a deterministic decision tree (ac_classifier.py); the LLM (qwen2.5-coder:7b)
         creates proposals, digests and audit
           flags — advisory-only, every action
           on them requires
         human (S5) approval.",

  store: "SQLite FTS5 corpus at /var/lib/vsf/rag-nucleus.db
                    — indexes ONLY experiments that
         passed vsl_run.py eval (all verdicts incl. FAIL/INCONCLUSIVE — FAILs are as informative as
         PASSes), spec.vsm + report.vsm, metadata (exp_id, verdict, ts). BM25 / sparse over a
         corpus of hundreds is right
           at this scale — no
           embeddings, no GPU, on the existing SQLite
         stack (revisit ≥ 1000 validated experiments)",
  ep: "Enriched Propose: vsl_run.py propose queries
                    the corpus (top-K BM25 over
                    the most similar
         past experiments) and injects REAL metric names, real binary paths, real protocol patterns
         into the prompt. Eliminates placeholders (stasis_cos ≥ 0.93, not metric_key ≥ value).",
  ac: "Algedonic Classifier — deterministic tree,
                    ms-latency, 23 unit tests, NO LLM (D4-L3).
         Read the tail of events.jsonl → a label (A=critical / B=warning / C=nominal) +
         alert.vsm; only writer of s5-alerts.db;
           never writes rag. Rules: viable:False→A;
         solve stasis_cos < 0.70 → A; < 0.80 → B; trust < 0.8 → B; regime ≠ recurrent → B;
         algedonic signal miss/status=critical → A;
           consecutive_warn ≥ 3 in window → B; invariant |x| ≥ 1e-3 → B;
           otherwise C. Asynchronous, non-blocking, advisory
           — the nucleus does not
         wait, and AC never closes
           a loop. Every failure path
           emits a deterministic class-B
         self-alert (monitor-the-monitor).",
  sd: "S5 Digest — periodic synthesis
                    of last-N AC alerts for
                    the human (one digest.vsm: patterns,
         trend, open conditions, ONE recommended action / no action). O1 only.",
  sa: "Semantic Auditor — LLM reads
                    coupling_registry + state.db censor +
                    report.vsm + metrics →
         flags ONLY logical contradictions (verdict×evidence, declared-dependency-censor
         mismatch, PASS-without-evidence): audit_flag.vsm → sa-audit.db; O1; runs at most once per
         5-min reconcile cycle.",
  ev: "Ethics Vigilance — O3-styled covenant-pattern
                    scan (three modes: post_hoc when the watchdog
         fired, novel_scan on clean cycles, canary_integrity on known violations) → outputs a
         typed s4_ethics_scan event. CANDIDATE_RULE flow: EV finds novel(could) → s4_ethics_scan →
         AC classifies (s4_ethics_candidate) → SD digest → human decides (adoption = D4 double-loop
         into the watchdog; dismissal only by an endorsed false) and returns.",
  store_isolation: "one CRAG store per function
                    (rag-, sa-audit-, s5-alerts- .db); strict
                    rules:
          no cross-script indexing; AC writes
            only s5-alerts; SA only sa-audit;
            SD may CROSS-READ
          (k < 3 fallback) but never cross-write; every system prompt declares it function + scope.",
  llm_transport: "on-demand via hardened qwen_client (tri-state
                    probe, cold-load budget, cooldown,
          storm guard, qwen.lock flock serialisation inside the LXC — FIFO, no daemon); Ollama
          restart authority lives ONLY in ensure_ollama (S3). File namespacing /tmp/qwen_<fn>_, req
          /resp",
  vsm_placement: "EP/SD = S4-proper (forward/projection); SA/EV = S3*-flavored within S4
         (backward/interpreting, LLM-reasoned); AC = deterministic signal-path (not advisory).
         Cybersyn map: store ≡ CHECO historical; AC ≡ Cyberfilter enrichment; EP ≡ environmental
         scan; SA/EV ≡ Cyberstride (semantic/ethics); SD ≡ Opsroom synthesis.",
  certified_gates: "boxes = connection_schema + G-V1..G-V4 (see view_contract §13 below) — the same
          validation loop the opsroom module
            uses.",
}

// ─── 11. S4 COGNITIVE / INTEGRATION spec — the in-kernel S4 channel (2026-06-21) ───
cog = {
  covenant_embedding: "rin compilation-time include_str!, build.rs computes
                    COVENANT_SHA256 from
         @covenant_production; verify_covenant() runs before every S4 prompt (the
         covenant cannot be bypassed without recompiling — which requires S5 approval).",

  channels: {
    phi_up:    "events.jsonl — S4 writes s4_ethics_scan / s4_ready / s4_offline; A0_classifier
                reads it on a cycle (ethics + angustia)",
    phi_down_s5:"/run/vsf/ethics_signal.json (tmpfs, TTL=30s), the deterministic
                    S5 watchdog path —
                LIVE",
    // debt(S4-PHIDOWN-INTEGRATION, class=kernel, owner=DS, gate=PHI-UP-PIPELINE)
    // φ↓ from S4 is written and ¬read. An ADVISORY channel nobody consumes
    // is a file, ¬a channel — and the recursive channel protocol requires an
    // L2 to emit a TYPED φ↑, which presumes the loop closes.
    phi_down_s4:"/run/vsf/s4_intelligence.json tmpfs, ADVISORY — the
                    kernel does not read it
                directly (integration pending)",
    tactical:  "VSL message via Motor2 →
                    cpu.weight (EXP-L1-01 Phase B, tutored) — the covenant /
                deterministic validator gates it",
  },

  S4_interface: "model qwen2.5-coder:7b, prompt = ⟦
                    COVENANT hash ⟧ + kernel
                    state + angustia signal
             + PSI level → 'suggest ONE support action (action_type|target|rationale)'. Response
             parses into a FIFO list: reduce_cpu_weight | request_cooldown | defer_task |
             escalate_human; the fallback on parse-fail
               or non-authorized action = log + no-op
             (safe default).",

  startup: "1) verify_covenant() — halt on
                    mismatch; 2) ping Ollama (model loaded); 3) emit
             s4_ready; 4) tail φ↑ for angustia. Fallback A_auto: on Ollama-down the S1 kernels
             operate autonomously with proven resilience.
             F_S4 holds D6: removing the LLM never breaks L0/L1.",

  s4_multi_s1: {
    context: "S4 functions (EP/AC/SD/SA→EV) today operate
                    on a single S1 domain
                    (vsf-nucleus).",
    target: "per-domain bundle over NATS vsf.{domain}.s4_context;
                    per-domain store rag-{domain}.db
             (isolation rule 6: identical to CRAG but per-domain); S4_SYNTH cross-domain synthesis
             (LLM = advisory; routing_signal that AC can classify B/A when urgency ≥ HIGH — only
             the routed signal triggers an algedonic; the synthesis itself is O1); store isolation
             rules 7-8: SYNTH reads all
               stores RO, s4_cross_domain_synthesis indexed to
               s5-alerts",
    d6_guard: "S4_SYNTH is advisory-only to the
                    human; routing_signal classified deterministically;
NO automated S3 action results
                from the LLM feed without human
               approval. Runs on
             deliberate minutes-cadence, not this tick (the network = AC).",
    confirmed_2026_07_02: "GATE MET — clima(LXC112, 23 services + 12 zones) +
                    econ(113, live copper
             feed) satisfy the historical first-external-S1 requirement; R6 cleared 2026-06-20.",
    deltas_2026_07_12: {
      1: "ALL new NATS code must use the token path: Rust via vsf_agent::nats::connect* (async-nats
             v_0.49.1 ignores URL auth), Python mirrors the working pattern (drop-ins with token).",
      2: "W2-BRIDGES-DONE: s4_clima_bridge + s4_markov_bridge are already systemd units
             (vsf-s4-clima-bridge.service / vsf-s4-markov-bridge.service), declared in state.db. So
             Phase1 reduces to ONE deliverable: the econ bundle bridge (vsf-s4-econ-bridge, systemd
             from the start — not a bare process).",
      3: "Ollama migrated to LXC 110 (10.10.20.110:11434, model qwen-2.5-coder:7b). The qwen.lock
             mutex must now cross-the-mesh (local file no longer shared) — resolve the OQ4:
             NATS carve lease or accept
               single-consumer cadence and skip the
               lock.",
      // debt(OLLAMA-UPGRADE-110, class=kernel, owner=DS, gate=system_certified)
      // num_ctx > 256 CRASHES on LXC 110, which hard-blocks Phase 2 (S4_SYNTH).
