// ─── 12. THE KERNEL BOUNDARY — OLLAMA DECOUPLE (R4/R10 — the LLM must never kill the kernel) ───
kernel_boundary: {
  diagnosis: "the original 'S4 blocks the
                    watchdog thread' hypothesis was PARTly
                    wrong: S4 runs on
             its own thread, the watchdog is a TOKIO task (10s keepalive) — the real kill
             vector was HOST CPU STARVATION (n02 = 2-core; ollama 110 with KEEP_ALIVE=-1 keeps two
             models resident, both doing CPU-only inference; live host load ≈ 7.76 over 2 cores) —
             the starved tokio runtime misses
               3 keepalives → systemd WatchdogSec=30s
               SIGKILL.",
  layers: {
    1_cpu_budget: "pct set 110 --cpulimit
      1 — cap ollama at
      1 core of the 2,
      reserve the other
                    for the watchdog/s3-star/clima liveness. Verify:
                      host load < ~3 under
                      inference.",
    2_single_model:"OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=5m — stop pinning BOTH
      models resident; accept cold-start on
                    the rarely-used model.",
    3_watchdog:    "move the keepalive to a DEDICATED OS thread (sleep loop) — it is the LAST thing
                    starved; has NO dependency on
                      the async runtime. Complement: WatchdogSec
                      30s→60s
                    to tolerate transient contention.",
    4_functional_degradation: "fast timeout on the S4 call (DS's fix), but S4 retries on its own
                    cadence — S4 is deliberative:
                      minutes are fine, always-fail is
                      not.",
  },
  significance: "R10 enforcement (an LLM can
                    never hold the kernel's liveness hostage) + explains
              the persistently weak S4 score
                — it was structurally mis-coupled on CPU-saturated
              hardware. Layers 1+3 = the
                safety fix; 2+4 make S4
                actually useful.",
}

// ─── 13. THE VIEW CONTRACT — certified φ↑ for the opsroom (v0.2.2) + retrofit honest-territory ───
view_contract = {
  laws: {
    validation_loop: "a contract is VALID only
                    if it (a) conforms to the pinned
                       @connection_schema version (reject on drift — G-V1) and (b) the
                       upstream source it projects is AX-STATE-certified + verified (G-V3). A
                       legacy interface is never adopted as a base (R9).",
    modularity: "the model is a HOST
                    for modules: they integrate/decommission cleanly; the panel
                       scaffold is ONE possible host,
                         not the abstraction.",
  },
  module_abstraction: "a self-describing module with an
                    explicit lifecycle (proposed → active
                    →
                       decommissioned). model≡reality: an active module with no live, verified feed
                       = ORPHAN (topology_reconcile catches); an uncommitted module emitting =
                       MISSING. The host renders ONLY declared + certified.",

  transport: "the φ↑ source is the
                    events.jsonl FILE (an axiomatic appendix,
                    chained, read-only
              bind-mount into the view-host) — NOT NATS. NATS Core is the ALGEDONIC carrier only
              (allowed). The browser never touches the source — the view-host projects it over a
              thin SSE.",

  certification_ownership: "certify the SOURCE (the nucleus
                    φ↑ — sign+chain attestation via the
              AX-STATE state_verify), not each projected frame: the view is a projection, so it
              re-signs every frame (costly + conceptually wrong). Certification happens at a
              periodic cadence (snapshot mode), the UI shows logo 'certified as of <ts>' on a
              green/red/grey — never blindly healthy.",

  gates: "G-V1 version pin; G-V2 conformance
                    (lifetime = ts + system_id
                    + source_ref; NO
          fabricated variety_delta / algedonic_seq /
            hash on a projection —
            those belong to the
          emitter); G-V3 attestation of the upstream source checkpoint (sig + chain +
          freshness); G-V4 declaration in coupling_registry (kind=phi_channel). A module failing
          any gate renders UNVERIFIED, never live.",

 retrofit_honesty: "VSF has no document-RAG pipeline
                    in code — so the
                    cybernetic diagram this
              retrofit describes is a RETROFIT: the S4-loop (A wrapper over a B retrieval
              primitive + homeostatic control) is STRUCTURAL. Most stages are PARTIAL (sparse, no
              dense embeddings; no re-ranker; the
                Ω-gate and lyapunov scored 'partial
                and novel at
              the substrate, aspirational coupling'). The GENUINE claim is narrow: the evaluation
              signal is a MEASURED dynamical-system metric (stasis_cos, Lyapunov dL, attractor
              convergence — Fierro-validated), not an LLM self-critique token; the gating Ω is a
              Σ-violation / covenant / signed-provenance
                boundary; the framing is home-C+VSM. The
              self-RAG/CRAG/agentic priors already did evaluation+correction
                on the GENERATION side
              (we do not claim that as novel): WE add measured DUAL stability + a formal feasible
              region + signed-provenance on top
                of the existing corrective loop.
                Do NOT draw the
              adaptive learning link as solid (aspirational G2) until the eval→weight symmetry is
              honestly instrumented. The view fields
                map: viability ← stasis_cos; in_omega
                ←
              Omega::canonical().violations(state).is_empty(); lyapunov ← Lyapunov controller dL
              per cycle; last_algedonic ← the
                NATS algedonic without fabricate consent.",
}

// ─── 13°. THE BEACON — network-level EVC of calibration (2026-07-03) ───
beacon: {
  insight: "the beacon is the NETWORK-level
                    application of 'calibrate-before-trust'. Axis-1
            calibrates instruments LOCALLY (2026-07-03); the beacon is where a node PROVES to the
            network that it is covenant-compliant
              AND its instruments are calibrated
              before it is
            trusted to participate — same
              principle as Core + EVC,
              one recursion up. Status 2026-07-03:
            RATIFIED: attestation protocol locked.",
  attestation: "trust root = the offline
                    S5 CA (ed25519 root, offline);
                    nodes sign a fixed
            kernel_birth payload { kernel_id, vsf_version, watermark, covenant_sha,
            calibration, cert } with their CA-issued key; the beacon PINs the S5-CA root pubkey.
            Verify: (1) cert chains to the pinned root; (2) sig verifies over the canonicalized
            payload; (3) covenant_sha == the beacon's current covenant sha; (4) [phase 2] the
            calibration hash matches a re-attestable
              census → PASS wears a
              TRUSTED registration,
            FAIL a REJECTED attempt + algedonic.",
  wiring: "on k2 startup the nucleus
                    POSTs the payload; retry/backoff; non-fatal
                    if the beacon is
            unreachable (announce-only, not a boot gate).",
  hardening: "behind Caddy (TLS + same
                    security headers), bind 127.0.0.1, systemd-managed — no more
            manual/nohup.",
  continuous_control: "a peripheral that failed silently
                    is a BLIND SPOT. REQUIRED: (1) DECLARE the
            beacon in the census + coupling registry; (2) probe end-to-end (port + GET /health 200
            + functional reachable from outside its host + registry writable) on a timer — EXERCISE
            the probe, do not assume; (3) N failures → beacon_down algedonic (high); (4) redundant
            channel (NATS-based registration) — an HTTP single is a SPOF.",
  general_principle: "every component, core AND peripheral,
                    must be DECLARED + HEALTH-PROBED
                    +
            algedonic-on-failure. A component that can
              die silently is an unregistered
              gap in the
            census — escalates to task(PERIPHERAL-HEALTH-CENSUS).",
}

