// ─── COMPLIANCE MAP (verdicts form) ───
// Every citation names canon
  items declared in boot/; the
  right side is this subsystem's verdict.
compliance:
  D6  = "LLM at the S4 layer
                    (L≥2) — the LLM is
                    advisory synthesis (EP/SD/SA), never a
             signal-classifier decision path (AC is deterministic; the algedonic stays LLM-free). OK."
  // D6-TACTICAL-UNDECLARED — CLOSED 2026-08-10 (rmw3, S5). Declared in
  // boot/vsl_language beside D6, and WIDENED past the LLM on his ruling:
  // the bands admit any non-deterministic proposer — LLM, ML, learned
  // modes. D6 governs the reflex band; D6.tactical governs the
  // deliberative one, guarded by @s5_policy_core §graduated_autonomy.
  // This block may now CITE D6.tactical as canon.
  // I NAMED D6.tactical here and declared it NOWHERE. It sits inside a
  // `compliance:` block, so it reads as a verdict — correctly — which leaves
  // the refinement itself undeclared: reflex/safety deterministic vs
  // deliberative tactical LLM-permitted under guards.
  // Either the canon adopts it (vsl_language, beside D6) or this document
  // stops naming it. Found by exporting the identifier index to RDF and
  // asking a graph engine which identifiers are cited and defined nowhere —
  // a question ∄ gate had ever asked.
  D6.tactical = "reflex/fast/safety = deterministic (OK); deliberative tactical
             = LLM-permitted under guards (consumer + graduated-autonomy rules
             in the S5 core). OK."
  // NAMESPACED 2026-08-09. The source wrote this as D6' — an ASCII apostrophe
  // reading as a PRIME, on a refinement the canon does not declare. Renaming it
  // to a bare D6 would have been WORSE: this is a document-local REFINEMENT of
  // the canonical D6 (LLM only at L ≥ 2), splitting its permission by reflex
  // vs deliberative, and a bare D6 would have redefined the canon rule in a
  // compliance table.
  // D6.tactical uses the suffix pattern the rubric already declares for
  // extensions of a canon item (A8.vOS, A12.vOS).
  // Caught on re-read after a mechanical sweep created exactly that collision
  // — which is the recertification clause doing its job on me.
  A5  = "pre-allocation stays within the envelope
                    (reallocation is zero-sum), loop gate to human
             on envelope/hardware/A5 changes — the
               machine never self-authorizes; double-looping
             policy stays human-owned. OK."
  D4  = "within-envelope = single-loop-automatable; donor-abuse/double-loop-upgrade =
                    pending_human
             — mechanical, flagged by the
               S3-star probe. OK."
  R4  = "every claim in this file
                    carries its live-verification evidence source
                    (cargo test output,
             is-active output, the S3* probe). The dual-component design (kernel claims vs host
             re-derives) is itself the independent check — R4 satisfied structurally. OK."
  R11 = "the reallocator, the probe, the
                    forecaster and the beacon are declared + named
             functionally — 'vsf-bbs-bridge' → 'vsf-s3-phidown-actuator' (it was never a BBS). OK."

